65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"- **Rin**: @Toshio, if we pick Free Address, I lose four to nine minutes every single morning. That is unacceptable.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, Free Address means no re-run costs, but it guarantees the morning chaos you fear. Fixed Desks cost once, then save time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Toshio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Toshio: @Rin, Free Address means no re-run costs, but it guarantees the morning chaos you fear. Fixed Desks cost once, then save time.""}]}"
67,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Rin, Free Address is unfair. The early arrivals would claim the window seats, leaving the rest of us in the dark.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, Free Address is a disaster. I need the quiet window side, and I won’t gamble on arriving early to get it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Mizuki, you’re right. If early birds grab the good spots, the rest of us are stuck in the dark. That’s not fair.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, Fixed Desks save my mornings, but who decides who gets the window? I need that choice to be fair, not first-come.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, Fixed Desks cost 6,200 yen once. Rotating Blocks cost it every shift. Stability is the only way to stop the bleeding.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Rin, Fixed Desks let us assign the window seats deliberately. We can ensure the quiet side isn’t hoarded, and the dark side is shared fairly.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, Fixed Desks are the only option that respects my physio note. I need a permanent spot to settle my chair, not a rotating one.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, I worry Fixed Desks freeze our connections. But if we group by function, maybe the joiners can still overhear the right people.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, if we group by function, do the new joiners still sit near the people who know the unwritten rules?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, Fixed Desks by Function groups similar work. It stabilizes the cost and the noise, which is what I can verify.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Toshio"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Toshio: @Rin, Fixed Desks by Function groups similar work. It stabilizes the cost and the noise, which is what I can verify.""}]}"
77,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"- **Mizuki**: @Rin, if we group by function, the joiners sit near the people who know the unwritten rules. That is the point.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Mizuki, grouping by function keeps me near the window. I accept Fixed Desks, provided my seat is permanently assigned.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Shion"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Shion: @Mizuki, grouping by function keeps me near the window. I accept Fixed Desks, provided my seat is permanently assigned.""}]}"
79,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, if the joiners sit near the right people, I can accept the fixed seats. I just need to know who gets the window side.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
